[UPDATED 2026-09-14] Out of date. The image with kubernetes/test-infra#37733 rolled out on 09-07 and the periodic kept failing. The failures are memory, and kubernetes/test-infra#37731 does not address them.

Current status as of 2026-08-28:

[test-infra#37733](https://github.com/kubernetes/test-infra/pull/37733) has merged and is the preferred generic fix for the outer runner process. It copies the effective parent cpu.max into the runner's init leaf, so quota-aware runtimes can see the same CPU ceiling that the kernel enforces.

The current `ci-kind-dra-1-34` definition still references `kubekins-e2e:v20260810-7619858115-1.34`, which predates that change. Therefore the periodic has not exercised the fix yet.

[test-infra#37731](https://github.com/kubernetes/test-infra/pull/37731) remains held as a fallback. The next gate is:

1. publish a kubekins image containing [test-infra#37733](https://github.com/kubernetes/test-infra/pull/37733);
2. update the release-1.34 job reference;
3. run the periodic repeatedly;
4. close [#37731](https://github.com/kubernetes/test-infra/pull/37731) if the job stabilizes.

The Go processes inside the nested kind nodes remain a separate question; [#37733](https://github.com/kubernetes/test-infra/pull/37733) intentionally does not assign CPU limits to those containers.

